WEBVTT

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:06.940
Japan!

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:12.410
In the seventeenth century, Tokugawa Iemitsu was shogun.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.790
The Yagyuu clan served as his covert operatives.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.830
So we should look into their family grave.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.540
There it is.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.280
Houtokuzenji Temple, in Nara.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.580
It's probably there...

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.090
Now there are only two left.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.040
Once we have all the sketches,

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.400
the girls will be...

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.630
Please!

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.370
I want to go to Kyoto, just for a day.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.430
Anna-san, I'd like that as well.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.680
Kyoto?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.810
I want to see where Papa grew up.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.820
Right now, Grandpa lives there by himself.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.840
Hocchii's never been able to visit him.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.070
I might be okay with going there too.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.490
Kaa-nee...

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.040
Wh-What?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.090
Why not?

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.330
There'll be time to look for the sketch later!

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:04.540
Sure.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.410
Huh?

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:06.640
What?

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.560
I said it's fine. What's with that reaction?

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.560
Well, you always say that the sketches take top priority.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.810
An occasional detour won't be a problem, right?

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.180
Or should I take it back?

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.050
Anna-san!

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.010
Grande Rosso!

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.940
Japanese!

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.640
Next stop, Kyoto.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:25.980
Wabi-sabi...

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.520
Classy!

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.020
And yummy traditional sweets!

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.480
Off to Kyoto!

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:50.580
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:50.580
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:58.380
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:58.380
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:05.640
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:05.640
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.730
shinkuromanika

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.730
Synchromanica

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.270
itsu no ma ni ka

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.270
Before I know it

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.440
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.440
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:18.740
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:18.740
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.240
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.240
I can hear someone's dream

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:32.210
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:32.210
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.010
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.010
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.350
shinkuromanika

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.350
Synchromanica

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.480
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.480
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.520
shinkuromanika

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.520
Synchromanica

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.740
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.740
The synchrony of your life

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.830
Japan

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.800
Hocchibi...

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.170
Let's go, already.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.630
Huh? I want to see more!

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.030
We can sightsee later.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.480
Hello!

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.310
Excuse us!

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.820
Who might you all be?

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.410
Grandpa! Long time, no see!

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.450
Oh, Hazuki?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.840
You've become such a beauty.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.570
I always was.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.740
Don't get ahead of yourself, Hazu-nee.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.000
So this must be Kazuki...
And you must be Hozuki.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.960
You remember?

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.880
Of course!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.200
But I'm surprised you've come all the way here.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.550
It's nice to meet you, Grandpa.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:05.200
Aw, you're such a cute girl.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.310
And you are...

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.600
My name is Anna Hendrix.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.810
I've been traveling with them since we left Italy.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.600
I see.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.890
Thank you for looking after my granddaughters.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.730
Well, don't be shy. Come on in!

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.490
Hocchii, take off your shoes.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.040
Oh, right.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.630
It's so cold.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.160
Oh, I forgot.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.560
Grandpa, do you always keep the heater off?

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.380
The price of fuel's skyrocketed,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.220
so it's not worth having on for just me.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.800
You shouldn't skimp on yourself.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.310
I'm accustomed to the cold.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.350
How are Geshio and the wife?

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.730
They're okay...

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:58.310
They decided we were old enough to take a trip by ourselves.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.650
That's pretty smart for Geshio.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.570
He always said he was too busy with work,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.920
no matter how often I told him to bring you over.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.330
Anna-san was with us, so we were fine.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.000
I see.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.830
Allow me to thank you again.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:21.700
Please... They've helped me more than I them.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.300
That's true...

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.430
I've covered for Anhedo-san a lot.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.510
Yeah, right.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.640
Kakkii, why you—

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.600
Right, Hocchibi?

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.930
Y-Yeah...

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.390
You're starting something, too, Hocchii?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.430
You little...

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.100
Hey, watch it!

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.440
Since you've come all this way,
why don't you stay for the night?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.690
Really?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:42.780
Of course.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.200
I'll go explore, then.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.570
Explore? Are you in elementary school?

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.950
Kakkii, you might run into ghosts.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.580
As if.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:55.290
It's bitter, but not bad.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:04.050
Simplicity and Frugality

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:04.050
The long trip here couldn't have been easy.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.470
Even if it's only for a day, you should relax.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.550
Thank you.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.640
What's this?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.020
Hocchii, over here.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.640
I found something interesting.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.760
Okay, be right there!

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.650
Papa's room?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:23.440
Let's see.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.860
First, the basics... Under his bed!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.490
I-Idiot, what are you doing?

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.610
What's the interesting find?

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.660
Shh!

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.280
Oh, what's this?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.790
Bingo, a photo album!

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.920
What's the matter?

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.170
That's Papa?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.050
He was in a band?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.690
How do you even read that name?

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.170
Let's see...

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.680
"Jet Engine"?

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:53.680
Lame!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.770
This dark past that ought to stay buried.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.560
Wow, he really was adrift for a while.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.900
Why did he settle on this look?

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.740
Maybe he got a job and wanted to straighten himself out?

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.360
I wouldn't call that straightening himself out.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.490
Yeah, it's weird.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.450
We're totally rejecting him.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.560
Haa-nee, look.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.150
What now?

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.790
At Kiyomizu Temple!!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.790
At Fushimi Inari

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.800
Arashiyama!!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.800
Kyoto Tower!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.800
Jump!!

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.800
Today's best photo!!

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.800
Just the
two of us...

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.800
Yum!!

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.890
They look happy.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.850
It's nice.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.310
Mama and Papa met,

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.270
and they got married...

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.690
That's why we're here, right?

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:49.570
Energy Converter

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.000
So that really was an energy converter, after all.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.100
That?

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:55.070
I think that's what all the ducts and
wires around the house are for.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.490
If it could be completed...

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.970
Hocchibi...

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.130
Can you do it?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.670
Yeah, probably.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.450
You really are good at this sort of thing.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.180
Okay, we'll leave the rest to you.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:17.930
Later.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:18.800
Okay.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.980
Grandpa, teach us to make Japanese food.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.060
Do you two like to cook?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:25.730
Yeah.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.650
Since we're here, we'd like to learn.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.480
I don't like it so much, but sure.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.920
You can probably start Hazu-nee off with the basics, like how to hold a knife.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.120
Shut up, Kakkii.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.740
Well, let's give this a try.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.130
You really suck.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.560
Just shut up.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.130
Let me have it.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:54.130
Oh, Kazuki has talent.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.340
I do?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.470
I hate to admit it, but that stew you made before was tasty, too.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.140
I just followed the recipe.

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.410
How's it going?

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.770
Pretty well.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:28.000
Two sketches left.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.920
And we have a pretty good idea where one is.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.130
I see.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.850
Say, Roberto...

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.090
What?

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.880
Once all the sketches have been found,

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.760
you won't need anything more from the girls, right?

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.760
Right.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.100
Then—

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.210
I'll dispose of them.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.020
Huh?

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:48.150
But last time...

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.650
Last time?

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.780
I'm only letting them go free until the sketches are found.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.290
Once that's done, I'll get rid of them, of course.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.160
R-Right...

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.280
Have you become attached?

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:03.190
Of course not.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.080
Contact me as soon as you've acquired the last of the sketches.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.290
Understood.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.800
This place feels kind of peaceful.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.510
We're part Japanese, after all.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.300
Here.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.970
Thanks.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.600
They call this roasted tea.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.320
Oh?

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.850
Ow, hot.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:32.810
I want to thank you for what you did.

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:33.820
Huh?

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.860
You saved us.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.140
That?

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.280
But...

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:45.490
If you hadn't done that, we would have all been killed.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.350
Yeah...

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.170
I just have a hard time forgiving myself

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:53.240
for giving in to a guy like him.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.600
Hazu-nee...

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:02.220
We just need to buy some missing parts and then make the final adjustments.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.300
Great job as usual, Hozuki-chan.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.390
Well, since we're here,

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.060
let's do some sightseeing while we shop.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.730
Really? We can do that?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.150
Yay!

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.440
That's what you've been wanting to do, right?

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.090
Yeah!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.610
But we can be your guards.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.990
Are you really going alone, boss?

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:28.640
Meeting a date with a crowd in tow is the epitome of bad manners.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.480
Look, look!

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:37.000
Maikos!

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.920
Awesome!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.940
It's the real thing!

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.340
Idiot...

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.590
You're way too excited.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.350
You're such a kid.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.720
I'm glad we came.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:48.970
Yes.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.950
I think they call these the Thousand Torii Gates.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.830
In total, there are more than five thousand.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.460
Five thousand?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.710
Kyoto is amazing!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.630
Omokaru

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.630
Stone

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.220
What did you wish for?

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.980
For your cooking to improve, even if only by a little bit.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.900
Women who cook are <i>so</i> last century!

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:37.900
Leave it.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:41.900
Actually, my wish was that we could all come here again someday.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.400
Kaa-nee...

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.910
Y-You have the wrong idea.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:50.830
I hope we can see Mama and Papa again.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.700
Yeah.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.160
We'll get home safely,

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:58.050
and we'll all come back with Mama and Papa.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.640
Anna-san?

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.720
Anna-san, are you okay?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.420
Huh?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.340
You look like you're in pain.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.720
Do you feel ill?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.760
No, I'm fine.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.430
Do I look like I'm getting sick?

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:18.690
Okay, let's split up and get this done.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.980
Don't get lost, you two.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.320
Right back at you, Hazu-nee.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.010
I'll be fine.

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:27.320
I've been here before.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.200
Later.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.960
I'm lost.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.370
Crap.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.790
I have to meet up with them fast.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.840
Hey, Bambina.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.490
I don't see her anywhere.

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:46.590
Man, where'd she go?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.630
Oh, look!

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:51.180
The <i>Ganymede</i>!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.350
Why in the world...

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.350
...are you here?

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:57.020
I heard you calling me.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.270
You know you're a stalker, right?

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.460
I'm glad.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.000
You're back to normal.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:02.730
Huh?

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.990
I heard that Messier bastard almost killed you.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.720
I couldn't just sit around, so I decided to come.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.030
Come with me,

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:12.780
Bambina.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.870
I can protect you.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:17.820
Huh?

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.080
Why are you acting all cool?

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.940
Don't laugh! I always mean what I say.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.920
Yeah, I know.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.050
Thanks.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:29.300
Well...

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:33.220
Then maybe I'll let you protect me...

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.380
Uh, wait a minute.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:36.350
Calm down.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.080
Are you serious? I'm an air pirate.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.730
I mean, that makes me happy, but... Well...

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.820
You should think things through.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.970
You're the one who suggested it.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.990
I'm so stupid.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.620
How can I talk about justice while I endanger my own sisters?

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.540
Hey...

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.080
Now that I've visited so many countries,

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:03.130
I know how powerless my "justice" really is.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.860
Just believing in the ideal justice

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:09.130
won't protect anything you really care about.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.350
Bambina...

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.860
Sticking to your ideals does take strength.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:24.750
But...

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:30.780
You shouldn't let people without principles hold all of the power.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.640
You don't need to change a damned thing about yourself.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.800
You're fine the way you are.

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:42.420
Just stay as you are.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.040
Huh?

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:49.210
Why are you acting so cool again?

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.930
Hey, I wasn't trying to be funny.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:55.640
Thanks.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.680
Somehow, that cheered me up.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:00.310
You might not be half bad, after all.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.440
It took you this long to realize that?

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.440
Hazu-nee!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.640
Once you have all of Galileo's inheritance,

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.530
I'll come and steal you, along with it.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.490
Just you wait, Bambina!

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.790
What was he doing here?

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.290
Who knows?

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.240
What's that supposed to mean?

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.610
We're back!

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:33.800
Welcome home.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.050
Today, we're having a hot pot.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.680
Oh, I've never tried hot pot before!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.430
I thought of you guys, and I made it a mix

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:45.370
of Japanese and Italian ingredients.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.690
Let's get right to it.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.030
Wait a moment.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.860
We'd like to show you something.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.120
Huh, what's that?

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:59.740
This looks like something Geshio drew in elementary school...

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.910
What a confusing scribble.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.820
Grandpa, please wait here.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.000
What's going on?

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:09.290
Will it work?

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.810
Here it comes.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.920
Uh, like this?

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.570
Oh? What's this?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:40.410
Haa-nee, Kaa-nee...

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.040
Did it work?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.560
Yup, perfectly!

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.920
The warm air feels nice.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.540
Yeah, the pipes and ducts that run throughout the house

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.300
are part of a temperature and humidity regulation system,

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.050
so you can always keep the climate comfortable.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:18:00.050
Not to mention that it's also designed to maximize energy efficiency.

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:02.810
You girls...

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:07.560
Grandpa, this is a gift to you from Papa and us.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:12.360
So this is what he was doing

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.730
around the time he began middle school.

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:19.070
He made enough of a racket that I thought the entire house was going to collapse.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:23.450
It may not look like much, but he had almost completed it.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.760
So he wasn't joking when he drew that.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:28.210
It definitely looks like he thought up the idea on a whim, though.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:31.960
I think he tried to turn the idea into a reality.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:37.330
He managed to build it partway,
but couldn't finish the thermal converter.

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:40.510
This is the best gift I've ever received.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.810
Thank you so much.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:46.600
I'll have to thank Geshio, too.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.820
It isn't such a big deal, Grandpa.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.690
Oh, is it ready?

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:52.700
I want to try it!

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:54.110
Oh, right!

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.150
I'm so excited!

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.640
Thanks for the food!

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:02.780
Thank you for helping with the cleanup.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:03.660
No problem.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.950
Thank you for the meal.

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:10.460
I suspect that this journey has been very difficult for my granddaughters.

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:15.510
But it seems to have been a good experience.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:19.330
Anna-san, I must thank you for that.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.290
Not really...

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:27.220
Please continue to look after them.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.560
Hey, there's no way that would work!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.570
No, it'll be fine... We can do it!

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.440
There!

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.150
H-Huh?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:43.780
What do you think you're doing?

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:49.540
Anna-san, thanks for today.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:50.620
Eh?

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:53.000
I was able to meet Grandpa,

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.540
and we also saw lots of great places.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:56.890
Hozuki-chan...

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:59.090
Grandpa was happy, as well.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.630
He said this bath used to only get lukewarm.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:07.560
Anhedo-san, if something is bothering you, just tell us.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.970
We're like family now.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:12.100
It's true.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.850
She's become like our oldest sister.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.440
You girls...

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:21.900
Hey, what?!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.860
Why are you crying?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.870
Thanks...

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.880
Okay, Grandpa. We'll be back some day.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.630
Bring the entire family next time.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.260
Okay!

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:43.070
See you, Grandpa.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.430
We'll be in Nara soon enough.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:54.460
Yagyuu, Yagyuu!

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:57.240
All right, let's go in.

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:00.710
We're going way into the mountains...

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.950
Yagyuu
Family
Grave
Site

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:04.930
This must be Yagyuu Munenori's grave.

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:09.200
Where's the usual fishy?

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:11.080
There it is!

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:14.160
We found it!

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.540
This is the fifth one!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:17.330
Only one more.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
